          0.0,
          0.0
        ],
        "visibility": 1,
        "opacity": 1.0,
        "locked": 0,
        "text": "Select more than one item and the Attribute Editor edits what they have in common. Try it on the three shapes.\n\n1   Drag a box around all three. A Shared attributes section appears in the Attribute Editor.\n2   Change Thickness once and every shape follows. “mixed” means the values differ.\n3   The ⇉ button gives the others the value of the item named in Values from. Right-click a row to apply it to every item of that type.\n4   Or copy the thick one (Ctrl+Alt+Shift+C), select the others and press Ctrl+Alt+Shift+V to choose what to paste.\n\nHere an attribute only needs the same name on the other items. A value that does not fit an item is skipped.",
        "color": [
          226,
          229,
          235
        ],
        "runs": null,
        "font_family": "",
